---
import GuideLayout from '../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { stories, storyHref, sections, sectionOf, isFree, minutes } from '../lib/stories';

const free = stories.filter(isFree);
const total = stories.length;
// Free stories have their own list above, so the groups hold the rest.
const groups = sections.map((g) => ({ ...g, stories: stories.filter((s) => !isFree(s) && sectionOf(s) === g.id) }));

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is a Bible sleep story?',
    a: 'A Bible sleep story is a calm, unhurried retelling of a passage of Scripture, read in a soft voice at a slow pace so you can listen with your eyes closed and drift off. It stays with the Bible account rather than inventing new plots, and each one names the passage it retells.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are Bible sleep stories for adults or children?',
    a: 'The stories in Bible Bedtimes are written for adults and for families winding down together. They are gentle enough for anyone to hear, but the pace and the language are designed for grown-up listeners rather than young children, so parents may want to listen first before sharing them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I listen to Bible sleep stories for free?',
    a: `Yes. Three complete stories are free in the Bible Bedtimes app: ${free.map((s) => s.title).join(', ')}. The rest of the ${total}-story library is part of the optional Premium subscription, and you can play a two-minute sample of any story first.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a sleep timer, and can I listen offline?',
    a: 'Yes to both. The app has a sleep timer, so the story stops on its own once you have fallen asleep. Premium members can also download story audio to listen without a connection, which helps if you keep your phone in airplane mode overnight.',
  },
];
---
<GuideLayout
  title={`Bible Sleep Stories for Adults — ${total} Calm Stories to Fall Asleep To | Bible Bedtime`}
  description={`Fall asleep to calm Bible stories: ${total} gentle retellings from Genesis to the Gospels, including hour-long listens, with a sleep timer. Three are free.`}
  eyebrow="Bible stories to fall asleep to"
  heading="Bible sleep stories for adults"
  intro={`Calm, faithful retellings of Scripture, read slowly so you can close your eyes and listen. There are ${total} stories in Bible Bedtimes, from Creation to the road to Emmaus, and three of them are free.`}
  crumb="Bible sleep stories"
  campaign="site_guide_sleep_stories"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <p>Many people find it easier to fall asleep listening than reading. A Bible sleep story gives your mind something good to rest on: a familiar account, told at a gentle pace, with no cliffhangers and nothing to stay awake for. Each story below is built around a passage you can look up and read for yourself.</p>

  <h2>Why listen to Bible stories at night?</h2>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li><strong>It quiets a busy mind.</strong> Following a story leaves less room for replaying the day.</li>
    <li><strong>It ends the day with Scripture.</strong> The last thing you hear is the faithfulness of God, not the news.</li>
    <li><strong>You can close your eyes.</strong> No screen to read, and a sleep timer stops the audio when you drift off.</li>
    <li><strong>It is familiar in a good way.</strong> Knowing how the story ends is part of what makes it restful.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="free">Three complete stories, free</h2>
  <p>Start with these. They are complete, not samples, and need no subscription.</p>
  <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
    {free.map((s) => (
      <li class="panel p-5 sm:p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">{s.reference} · {minutes(s)} min · Free</p>
        <h3 class="!mt-2"><a href={storyHref(s)} class="hover:text-gold-light">{s.title}</a></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-cream/75 leading-relaxed">{s.description}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section id={g.id} class="scroll-mt-24">
      <h2>{g.title}</h2>
      <p>{g.note}</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 divide-y divide-white/[0.08] border-y border-white/[0.08]">
        {g.stories.map((s) => (
          <li class="py-5">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
              <h3 class="!mt-0 !text-[22px]"><a href={storyHref(s)} class="hover:text-gold-light">{s.title}</a></h3>
              <span class="text-sm text-cream/60">{s.reference} · {minutes(s)} min</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-2 text-cream/70 leading-relaxed">{s.description}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>
  ))}
  <p class="!mt-6 text-sm text-cream/60">Premium stories include a two-minute sample you can play before deciding on Premium. The library grows over time; this list reflects the app catalogue on 18 September 2026. Each story has its own page with the passage, its length and a short KJV reading: see <a class="inline" href="/stories/">all {total} stories</a>.</p>

  <h2>How to fall asleep to a Bible story</h2>
  <ul class="bullets">
    <li><strong>Set the sleep timer first</strong> so you are not reaching for your phone later.</li>
    <li><strong>Turn the brightness down</strong> and put the phone face down once the story starts.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick a story you already know.</strong> Familiar stories are easier to relax into than new ones.</li>
    <li><strong>On restless nights, choose an hour-long listen</strong> so the voice carries on while you settle.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Prefer to read? Try our <a class="inline" href="/psalms-for-sleep/">psalms for sleep</a> or <a class="inline" href="/bible-verses-for-sleep/">Bible verses for sleep</a>.</p>
</GuideLayout>
